                    <occupation>Money Scrivener</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> John Abbott appears at 6 Poland Street in the rate books of 1774.
                            According to the Daily Advertiser on 25 July 1774, his assignees were
                            handling the sale of his effects and lease, suggesting that he was
                            declared bankrupt in 1774. He is described as a money scrivener, living
                            in St James parish on the east side of Poland Street near Great
                            Marlborough Street. Listed in the Law List of 1779 as John Abbot of
                            Poland Street. </p>
